# Cloud Functions configuration. Copy to functions/.env for local development.
#
# The emulator defaults work as-is; nothing here needs setting to run the
# project locally. Both values matter in a real deployment.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage bucket
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The bucket holding report photographs. Must match
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET in the mobile app's .env — if the two
# disagree, account deletion reports success having deleted no photographs and
# the orphan sweep finds nothing to do, silently and for ever.
#
# Leave unset to use "<project-id>.firebasestorage.app", which is what Firebase
# projects created from late 2024 onwards get. **Set it explicitly if your
# project's bucket is on the older <project-id>.appspot.com domain** — the
# Admin SDK's own default is the .appspot.com form, and it does not error on
# the wrong name, it just returns an empty bucket.
#
# STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project-id.appspot.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Places (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Places key is a *secret*, not an environment variable, so it does NOT
# belong in this file. Set it with:
#
#   firebase functions:secrets:set GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY
#
# For the emulator, put it in functions/.secret.local (git-ignored):
#
#   GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=your-key-here
#
# Without it, nearbyPlacesProxy returns failed-precondition and the app falls
# back to OpenStreetMap, which is the default configuration this repository
# ships. See docs/nearby-places.md.
